(Regression test: per-slot type tags must survive _list_append
 reallocation. An empty list literal starts with capacity 8; appending
 past that triggers the realloc path, which must copy the tag bytes to
 the new block alongside the values - otherwise the early string and
 float elements would print as raw integers after growth.)

a list called "stuff" is [].
append 10 to stuff.
append "eleven" to stuff.
append 12.5 to stuff.
append yes to stuff.
a number called "i" is 1.
While i is less than or equal to 9, append i to stuff, increment i.

Print "len: {stuff's length}".
For each s in stuff, print s.
Print stuff's first.
Print stuff's last.
Print element 2 of stuff.
Print element 3 of stuff.
